 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Schottky barrier power diode with a large-area metal-to-silicon junction, epitaxial construction, an oxide-passivated junction, a metal overlay contact and a guard ring for stress protection. It withstands reverse avalanche energy transients and passes ISO 7637 pulse 1 (5000 pulses at 100 V, 10 Ω)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Choosing a part",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The six parts carry the same current, surge, thermal and forward-voltage ratings and differ in reverse voltage (20, 30 or 40 V) and qualification. SBRS8320T3G, NRVBS330T3G and SBRS8340T3G are AEC-Q101 qualified and PPAP capable, for automotive and other uses with unique site and change-control requirements."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "With RθJL = 11 °C/W at 20 kHz, the allowed average current is about 4.7 A dc up to a lead temperature near 122 °C and 3.0 A with a square wave up to 130 °C; both fall to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
